{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RevocationFeed"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"What this narrows, and what it is not","anchor":"What-this-narrows-and-what-it-is-not","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An AXIAM access token is self-contained and valid for up to fifteen minutes, and this SDK","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"verifies it locally. A logout, a role removal or an account disable therefore does not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reach a token already in a caller’s hands until it expires — §10.2 records that, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"documented answer has been “route the decision through gRPC introspection instead”, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is correct and costs a round trip ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"per request","type":"text"}]},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A deployment may publish "},{"code":"GET \/oauth2\/revocations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": the base64url-unpadded SHA-256 of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every session id revoked within the last access-token lifetime. A guard that polls it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rejects a revoked session within "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one poll interval","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of one token lifetime, for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one cacheable fetch per interval."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is NOT a control, and every rule below follows from that:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Default off."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Nothing polls unless a caller constructs one and attaches it."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Never on the request path."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/isRevoked(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" answers from the cached set and, at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"most, refreshes a set the "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"next"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" caller sees."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Never fail closed.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" An unreachable feed, a non-"},{"code":"200","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a body that does not parse, an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"alg","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" this build does not know — every one of them behaves exactly as no feed at all."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Not as an empty list: an empty list asserts that nothing has been revoked, which is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"guard that silently honours no revocations while appearing to honour them."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"It only ever rejects.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" Every §10.1 rule runs first and still decides. The feed can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"turn an accept into a reject and never the reverse.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A token with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sid"},{"type":"text","text":" is never matched."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" There is no session behind a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"client-credentials token, an RPT or a token exchange, and hashing ","type":"text"},{"code":"jti","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"match nothing while looking like it worked.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actor"},{"type":"text","text":", so one instance can be shared across guards and they poll once between them"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than once each. Callers do not build one directly: set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamConfig\/revocationFeedEnabled","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" wires it to the same transport"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every other call already uses."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The optional session-revocation feed poller (CONTRACT.md §10.4, contract 1.44 — AXIAM"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"threats T-39 and T-143)."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/revocationfeed"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/ScA","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/12_Concurrency8AnyActorP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Class","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"class","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RevocationFeed"}],"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK14RevocationFeedC","navigatorTitle":[